# Writing style

## No em dashes

Never use the em dash character (`—`, U+2014) in anything you write for this project.

Applies to chat replies, commit messages, PR descriptions, UI strings (`Strings*.resx`), help HTML, README, TODO notes, code comments, and XML docs.

| Avoid | Use |
|-------|-----|
| em dash (`—`) | comma, colon, parentheses, or a full stop and a new sentence |
| spaced hyphen as a fake em dash (` - `) for asides | commas or parentheses |

Unicode minus (`−`) for negative numbers (for example −1°) is fine. En dashes in numeric ranges are fine if the surrounding style already uses them; do not replace them with em dashes.

```text
Bad:  Happy path reads can stay lock-free — rebuild stays under the lock.
Good: Happy path reads can stay lock-free. Rebuild stays under the lock.
Good: Happy path reads can stay lock-free (rebuild stays under the lock).
```

## No ellipsis in titles

Never use `...` or `…` in titles. Finish the thought with a complete phrase.

Applies to:

- Commit subject lines and PR titles
- Window, dialogue, section, and menu titles
- Help page `<title>` / headings used as titles
- Localisation keys that are titles (for example `*.Title`)

Status or progress copy in body text may still use ellipsis when it means “in progress” (for example “Testing connection…”). That must not appear in a title.

```text
Bad:  Add satellite status reporting...
Good: Add OscarWatch.org satellite status reporting with optional QSO auto-On.
```

When editing existing text that breaks these rules, fix the lines you touch. Do not sweep the whole repo unless asked.
